1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,000
We can now ask a machine a question

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,850
and receive an answer in seconds.

3
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:11,175
But the hardest questions did not disappear.

4
00:00:11,175 --> 00:00:14,025
Where did this conclusion come from?

5
00:00:14,025 --> 00:00:15,925
Which premises carry it?

6
00:00:15,925 --> 00:00:18,775
What is the strongest live objection?

7
00:00:18,775 --> 00:00:22,575
And if the answer changes tomorrow, who can

8
00:00:22,575 --> 00:00:24,000
still see why?

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,885
Publishing made information abundant.

10
00:00:28,885 --> 00:00:30,570
Search made it retrievable.

11
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:32,676
Generative AI made synthesis instantaneous.

12
00:00:32,676 --> 00:00:36,045
Yet the structure behind an answer remains scattered

13
00:00:36,045 --> 00:00:38,994
across pages, footnotes, comments, and overwritten revisions.

14
00:00:38,994 --> 00:00:42,364
A reader still has to rebuild the dependency

15
00:00:42,364 --> 00:00:45,733
graph by hand: the definition in use, the

16
00:00:45,733 --> 00:00:49,103
independent evidence, the hidden assumption, the counterexample, and

17
00:00:49,103 --> 00:00:52,052
the moment a prior conclusion stopped holding.

18
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:55,000
Knowledge Ball begins at that unresolved layer.

19
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,744
It is not another answer engine.

20
00:01:00,744 --> 00:01:04,136
It is a spatial, versioned knowledge network designed

21
00:01:04,136 --> 00:01:07,528
to make claims inspectable, challengeable, revisable, and learnable.

22
00:01:07,528 --> 00:01:10,496
A durable Knowledge Node keeps its identity.

23
00:01:10,496 --> 00:01:13,888
A Claim Version records one assertion at one

24
00:01:13,888 --> 00:01:15,160
point in time.

25
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:18,552
A Reasoning Node binds explicit premises to one

26
00:01:18,552 --> 00:01:19,400
concrete conclusion.

27
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:22,792
A material change creates a new version; it

28
00:01:22,792 --> 00:01:25,760
does not silently overwrite the old one.

29
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:27,032
Names remain labels.

30
00:01:27,032 --> 00:01:30,000
Identity, lineage, and relationships carry the history.

31
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,067
Those relationships become space.

32
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:38,800
The cyan inner shell holds definitions, facts, and

33
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:39,733
logic symbols.

34
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:43,467
The blue middle shell holds other admitted public

35
00:01:43,467 --> 00:01:43,933
knowledge.

36
00:01:43,933 --> 00:01:47,667
The violet outer shell holds pending, disputed, predictive,

37
00:01:47,667 --> 00:01:49,067
and value-laden content.

38
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:50,933
Geometry is not decoration.

39
00:01:50,933 --> 00:01:52,800
Shells encode semantic status.

40
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,200
Chains encode dependency.

41
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,533
Deterministic placement protects spatial memory.

42
00:01:56,533 --> 00:02:00,267
The interface leads with overview, then relationships, then

43
00:02:00,267 --> 00:02:04,000
full content when the user zooms or focuses.

44
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,873
Creation is not acceptance.

45
00:02:08,873 --> 00:02:12,218
Under the committed protocol design, a candidate is

46
00:02:12,218 --> 00:02:15,564
checked for reference integrity, legal relations, cycles, duplicate

47
00:02:15,564 --> 00:02:17,655
risk, and real semantic change.

48
00:02:17,655 --> 00:02:21,000
Support and opposition stake against that exact version.

49
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,345
The first side to reach the current eligibility-adjusted

50
00:02:24,345 --> 00:02:26,436
threshold produces a bounded verdict.

51
00:02:26,436 --> 00:02:27,273
Bounded matters.

52
00:02:27,273 --> 00:02:30,618
Correct means currently accepted under a known evidence

53
00:02:30,618 --> 00:02:33,964
set and rule set—not eternal truth, and not

54
00:02:33,964 --> 00:02:35,636
truth manufactured by popularity.

55
00:02:35,636 --> 00:02:38,982
New evidence can create a new version or

56
00:02:38,982 --> 00:02:39,818
opposing branch.

57
00:02:39,818 --> 00:02:43,164
The active view may change while admitted history

58
00:02:43,164 --> 00:02:44,000
remains auditable.

59
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:50,296
Energy gives judgment a cost, but it is

60
00:02:50,296 --> 00:02:53,392
not a token launch and it is not

61
00:02:53,392 --> 00:02:54,553
external financial value.

62
00:02:54,553 --> 00:02:57,649
In the current design, submitting a candidate, supporting

63
00:02:57,649 --> 00:03:00,745
it, or opposing it each locks one unit

64
00:03:00,745 --> 00:03:02,294
against a specific version.

65
00:03:02,294 --> 00:03:03,842
Settlement follows double-entry accounting.

66
00:03:03,842 --> 00:03:06,938
Every internal transfer balances, and global net Energy

67
00:03:06,938 --> 00:03:07,712
remains zero.

68
00:03:07,712 --> 00:03:09,260
The ledger is authoritative.

69
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:12,356
A client may request an action and display

70
00:03:12,356 --> 00:03:15,452
the result; it may never declare a balance

71
00:03:15,452 --> 00:03:17,000
or perform privileged settlement.

72
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:22,600
One network, two strictly separated questions.

73
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:25,800
Public knowledge asks: what version does the protocol

74
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,400
currently accept, and why?

75
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:30,600
Private mastery asks: what have I seen, understood,

76
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,200
saved, illuminated, or hidden?

77
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:35,400
Personal state does not enter public voting, public

78
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,000
events, or public accuracy.

79
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,200
Hiding a conclusion in personal mode can hide

80
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:43,000
its reasoning without rewriting the shared graph.

81
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Visitors may inspect public knowledge.

82
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,200
Public changes still pass through identity, permission, and

83
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,000
protocol boundaries.

84
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:55,218
The working prototype is built with TypeScript, Vite,

85
00:03:55,218 --> 00:03:55,972
and Three.

86
00:03:55,972 --> 00:03:58,990
js, with the web implementation shared into Android

87
00:03:58,990 --> 00:04:00,122
and Windows packages.

88
00:04:00,122 --> 00:04:03,139
The backend direction uses Supabase and Postgres for

89
00:04:03,139 --> 00:04:06,157
identity, events, the Energy ledger, and row-level security.

90
00:04:06,157 --> 00:04:08,797
The server—not the visualization—is the authority boundary.

91
00:04:08,797 --> 00:04:11,815
The practical starting points are bounded domains: learning

92
00:04:11,815 --> 00:04:14,833
maps, research synthesis, organizational decisions, and structured context

93
00:04:14,833 --> 00:04:15,587
for AI.

94
00:04:15,587 --> 00:04:18,228
Models may extract candidate claims and relationships.

95
00:04:18,228 --> 00:04:19,359
People confirm intent.

96
00:04:19,359 --> 00:04:22,000
The protocol, not the model, decides admission.

97
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:28,216
As of White Paper one point zero, Knowledge

98
00:04:28,216 --> 00:04:31,232
Ball is a working prototype with a converging

99
00:04:31,232 --> 00:04:33,494
protocol—not infrastructure proven at internet scale.

100
00:04:33,494 --> 00:04:35,002
The theory is coherent.

101
00:04:35,002 --> 00:04:36,510
Engineering viability is moderate.

102
00:04:36,510 --> 00:04:38,018
Commercial value remains unproven.

103
00:04:38,018 --> 00:04:41,034
Large-scale operation still needs evidence: stronger identity, domain

104
00:04:41,034 --> 00:04:44,051
governance, source quality, deterministic layout, recovery, and sustained

105
00:04:44,051 --> 00:04:44,805
mobile performance.

106
00:04:44,805 --> 00:04:47,444
That honesty is part of the product.

107
00:04:47,444 --> 00:04:48,575
Knowledge is energy.

108
00:04:48,575 --> 00:04:50,460
Every conclusion can be questioned.

109
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:52,345
Every revision leaves a reason.

110
00:04:52,345 --> 00:04:55,361
Every person can see the real distance between

111
00:04:55,361 --> 00:04:58,000
themselves and what they want to know.
